### 1.4 Variables (§1.3 extraction)
1. Object set — per-object kind (die/house/minidie/cube), position in bowl-relative coords, size, rotation, pip count, collapse-stroke assignment. Counts per kind derived from the array.
2. Collapse law — per-stroke cohort sizes, integrity span (loss inside the assigned stroke), deform coefficients (shrink, corner-rounding, colour blend to paste, sink), fleck size/count (collapsed objects persist as flecks of their own colour).
3. Paste — start coverage, per-stroke coverage growth, paste colours (base/dark), blob geometry (coverage rendered as growing paste field under/over objects).
4. Pestle — geometry (head radii, handle), rest position, raised position, per-stroke target sweep, dip depth, stroke phase split (press vs lift).
5. Bowl/stage — bowl centre/radii, wall colours, board palette, stage size.
6. Labels — input label text, tool label text, output label text, font sizes + family, label positions.
7. Timing — setup duration, stroke count, stroke duration, final hold; phase starts DERIVED sequentially. Stop-motion quantum (stepMs) — the increment size.
8. Palette — board, bowl, paste ×2, die, house, minidie, cube, pestle, ink.
9. Easing — stroke easing name.

